  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000230">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A compensator is a material artifact that has the designed function of compensating for axial or radial movement between two connected elements.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">compensador</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">compensator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b459"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um compensador é um artefato material que tem a função projetada de compensar movimento axial ou radial entre dois elementos conectados.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A compensator is a material artifact that has the designed function of compensating for axial or radial movement between two connected elements.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b455"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000099">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A butterfly control valve is a control valve that has a rotating disc closure mechanism and bears a process-controlled flow function enabling automated flow modulation in response to external control signals.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula borboleta de controle é uma válvula de controle que possui um mecanismo de fechamento por disco rotativo e possui uma função de fluxo controlado por processo, permitindo modulação automatizada do fluxo em resposta a sinais de controle externos.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula borboleta de controle</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">butterfly control valve</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b269"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000087"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b268"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every butterfly control valve is a valve that has-component-part-at-all-times some rotating disc and has-component-part-at-all-times some actuator and bearer-of some process-controlled flow function.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(ButterflyControlValve(x) → Valve(x) ∧ ∃d(RotatingDisc(d) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,d)) ∧ ∃a(Actuator(a) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,a)) ∧ ∃f(ProcessControlledFlowFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A butterfly control valve is a control valve that has a rotating disc closure mechanism and bears a process-controlled flow function enabling automated flow modulation in response to external control signals.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">This is a constructive type that combines two existing differentia (butterfly mechanism + control function). Under OWA, providing sufficient conditions could lead to false positives where any valve with both a rotating disc and control capability would be classified as this specific type, even if it has additional specialized features or hybrid mechanisms.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b534">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b536"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000287">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma junta é um artefato material feito de material deformável arranjado em loops fechados que possui uma função de vedação para prevenir vazamentos entre superfícies de acoplamento com movimento relativo limitado.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A gasket is a material artifact made of deformable material arranged in closed loops that bears a sealing function to prevent leakage between mating surfaces with limited relative movement.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive basis (CLAUDE.md): the definition constrains material and geometry — deformable material arranged in closed loops — not function alone. As equivalent it made MaterialArtifact + SealingFunction sufficient for gasket-hood, so every sealing artifact was inferred to be a gasket. Those constructive conditions live only in differentia_expression and do not reach the OWL, so equivalence asserted far more than intended.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A gasket is a material artifact made of deformable material arranged in closed loops that bears a sealing function to prevent leakage between mating surfaces with limited relative movement.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1254"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every gasket is a material artifact that has component part some deformable material and bears some sealing function and has property some closed loop geometry.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Gasket(x) ↔ MaterialArtifact(x) ∧ ∃f(SealingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃m(DeformableMaterial(m) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,m)) ∧ ∃g(ClosedLoopGeometry(g) ∧ hasProperty(x,g)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">junta</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gasket</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000517">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de vaporização flash</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flash vaporization function</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the partial vaporisation of a pressurised liquid stream caused by a rapid reduction in pressure.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1091"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1090"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b522">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000445"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b486">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000437"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000427">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b314"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b315"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de proteção catódica</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cathodic protection function</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the prevention of electrochemical corrosion of a metallic structure by making it the cathode of an electrochemical cell.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000690">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de queima de gás residual</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">waste gas burning process</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which surplus or waste gas is combusted in a flare or incinerator to destroy it safely and prevent atmospheric venting.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1076"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1075"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1861">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000530"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000334">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A pressure indicating transmitter is a transmitter that measures pressure and provides both local visual indication and electrical signal transmission of the pressure value.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um transmissor indicador de pressão é um transmissor que mede pressão e fornece tanto indicação visual local quanto transmissão de sinal elétrico do valor da pressão.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every pressure indicating transmitter is a transmitter that bears a pressure indicating and transmission function, has pressure signal as input, and has both electrical signal output and local pressure display.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2018"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">transmissor indicador de pressão</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pressure indicating transmitter</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (PressureIndicatingTransmitter(x) ↔ Transmitter(x) ∧ ∃f(PressureIndicatingAndTransmissionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃i(PressureMeasurementResult(i) ∧ hasInput(x,i)) ∧ ∃o1(InformationContentEntity(o1) ∧ hasOutput(x,o1)) ∧ ∃o2(PressureMeasurementResult(o2) ∧ hasOutput(x,o2)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A pressure indicating transmitter is a transmitter that measures pressure and provides both local visual indication and electrical signal transmission of the pressure value.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2151">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000610"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000675">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de suporte e conexão de coluna de produção</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tubing support and connection function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2519"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2518"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes both the mechanical support of tubing strings within a wellbore and their connection to surface or subsurface equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000098">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A blower is a compressor that compresses and supplies air or gas at medium pressure and medium volume flow.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every blower is a compressor that has the function of compressing gas and operates at medium pressure and medium volume flow ranges.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (Blower(x) ↔ (Compressor(x) ∧ ∃f,p,v (CompressionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f) ∧ MediumPressureRange(p) ∧ MediumVolumeFlowRange(v) ∧ hasOperatingParameter(x,p) ∧ hasOperatingParameter(x,v))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A blower is a compressor that compresses and supplies air or gas at medium pressure and medium volume flow.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um soprador é um compressor que comprime e fornece ar ou gás em pressão média e vazão volumétrica média.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">soprador</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">blower</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000073"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b216"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Blower</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">BLOWER</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000268">
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every filter press is a filter that has a pressure mechanism as part and participates in mechanical compression processes.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A filter press is a filter that applies mechanical compression force to enhance the separation of substances through a pressurized filtration process.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">filter press</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">prensa filtrante</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma prensa filtrante é um filtro que aplica força de compressão mecânica para melhorar a separação de substâncias através de um processo de filtração pressurizada.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A filter press is a filter that applies mechanical compression force to enhance the separation of substances through a pressurized filtration process.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions because this is classified as 'both' functional and constructive. The structural differentia (pressure mechanism and compression process) involves specific mechanical configurations that are harder to make sufficient under Open World Assumption without detailed engineering specifications.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b996"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000081"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b997"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(FilterPress(x) → Filter(x) ∧ ∃p(PressureMechanism(p) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,p)) ∧ ∃proc(MechanicalCompressionProcess(proc) ∧ participatesIn(x,proc)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000074">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A shell and tube heat exchanger is a heat exchanger that has a tube bundle spatially contained within a surrounding shell.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">shell and tube heat exchanger</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">trocador de calor de casco e tubos</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A shell and tube heat exchanger is a heat exchanger that has a tube bundle spatially contained within a surrounding shell.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um trocador de calor de casco e tubos é um trocador de calor que possui um feixe de tubos contido espacialmente dentro de um casco envolvente.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2271"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000092"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2270"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2269"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">ShellAndTubeHeatExchanger(x) → HeatExchanger(x) ∧ ∃tb(TubeBundle(tb) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,tb)) ∧ ∃s(Shell(s) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,s) ∧ spatiallyContains(s,tb))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every shell and tube heat exchanger is a heat exchanger that has a tube bundle as component part and has a shell as component part, where the tube bundle is spatially contained within the shell.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions for this constructive type to avoid false positives under OWA. Any equipment with a shell and tube bundle could theoretically be classified as a standard shell-and-tube heat exchanger, but specialized variants (like graphite shell-and-tube or custom multi-stream designs) should not be automatically forced into this maintenance category without domain expert validation.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000307">
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1541"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1542"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000092"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um refervedor tipo kettle é um refervedor que possui orientação horizontal e contém um espaço de vapor separado para desengajamento vapor-líquido.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A kettle reboiler is a reboiler that has horizontal orientation and contains a separate vapour space for vapor-liquid disengagement.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A kettle reboiler is a reboiler that has horizontal orientation and contains a separate vapour space for vapor-liquid disengagement.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">kettle reboiler</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">refervedor tipo kettle</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type defined by specific physical configuration. Under Open World Assumption, sufficient conditions could incorrectly classify equipment with horizontal orientation and vapor space but fundamentally different purposes (e.g., horizontal separators, flash drums) as kettle reboilers. The structural differentia provides necessary conditions for the kettle reboiler maintenance/procurement category.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every kettle reboiler is a reboiler that has horizontal orientation and has a separate vapour space as component part.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(KettleReboiler(x) → Reboiler(x) ∧ ∃q(HorizontalOrientation(q) ∧ hasQuality(x,q)) ∧ ∃v(SeparateVapourSpace(v) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,v)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b997">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/FilterMedium"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasComponentPartAtAllTimes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b417">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000431"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1800">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1802"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000153">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula de retenção basculante</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">swing check valve</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula de retenção basculante é uma válvula de retenção que possui um elemento de fechamento consistindo de um disco que gira livremente em um mecanismo de dobradiça e abre automaticamente quando o fluxo é estabelecido e fecha automaticamente quando o fluxo cessa ou se inverte.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A swing check valve is a check valve that has a closure member consisting of a disc which swings freely on a hinge mechanism and opens automatically when flow is established and closes automatically when flow ceases or reverses.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A swing check valve is a check valve that has a closure member consisting of a disc which swings freely on a hinge mechanism and opens automatically when flow is established and closes automatically when flow ceases or reverses.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000103"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2376"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions for this constructive type to avoid false positives under OWA. Any artifact with a hinged disc mechanism should not automatically be classified as a swing check valve without domain expert validation, as specialized equipment may contain swing mechanisms but serve different primary functions.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(SwingCheckValve(x) → CheckValve(x) ∧ ∃d(HingedDisc(d) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,d)) ∧ ∃a(SwingArm(a) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,a)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every swing check valve is a check valve that has a hinged disc as component part and has a swing arm as component part</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000515">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1035"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1036"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000465"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de detecção de chama</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flame detection function</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A detection function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the sensing of the presence of a flame or combustion event by detecting radiant energy or other combustion signatures.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000606">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2014"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2013"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pressure indicating and transmission function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de indicação e transmissão de pressão</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the measurement of process pressure and both its local display and the transmission of the corresponding signal to a remote monitoring system.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1439">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000551"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b764">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/InformationContentEntity"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000239">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">amortecedor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">damper</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A damper is an assembly that bears the designed function to suppress, regulate, or reduce unfavorable dynamic characteristics such as vibrations, pressure fluctuations, or flow disturbances.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um amortecedor é um conjunto que possui a função projetada de suprimir, regular ou reduzir características dinâmicas desfavoráveis como vibrações, flutuações de pressão ou distúrbios de fluxo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A damper is an assembly that bears the designed function to suppress, regulate, or reduce unfavorable dynamic characteristics such as vibrations, pressure fluctuations, or flow disturbances.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b573"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b481">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000039"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000428">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which electrochemical corrosion of a metallic structure is prevented by making it the cathode of an electrochemical cell through the supply of electrical current or sacrificial anodes.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cathodic protection process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de proteção catódica</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b316"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b317"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000478">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which fluid flow is redirected from one path to one or more alternative downstream paths by petroleum production equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">diverting process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de desvio de fluxo</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b822"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b821"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000185">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the measurement and remote transmission of the flow rate of a process stream.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1165"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000030"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1164"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de transmissão de sinal de fluxo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flow signal transmission function</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000333">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A FiatObjectPart that is the secondary winding of a power transformer and that bears a SecondaryWindingFunction consisting in delivering transformed electrical power at the output voltage level.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A FiatObjectPart that is the secondary winding of a power transformer and that bears a SecondaryWindingFunction consisting in delivering transformed electrical power at the output voltage level.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma FiatObjectPart que é o enrolamento secundário de um transformador de potência e que possui uma SecondaryWindingFunction consistindo em fornecer energia elétrica transformada no nível de tensão de saída.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">enrolamento secundário de transformador de potência</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">power transformer secondary winding</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1984"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1985"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification basis - the physical configuration (being the secondary winding of a power transformer) provides necessary conditions, but sufficient conditions are harder to assert under OWA without risking false positives for specialized or hybrid transformer configurations.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000545">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b948"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b947"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de movimentação de gás</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gas movement process</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which gas is transported from one location to another by imparting kinetic or pressure energy to the gas stream.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000145">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula de alívio</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">relief valve</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A relief valve is a valve that is designed to automatically open at a predetermined pressure setpoint to relieve excess pressure and prevent unsafe pressure levels in a system.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2107"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula de alívio é uma válvula projetada para abrir automaticamente em um ponto de ajuste de pressão predeterminado para aliviar o excesso de pressão e prevenir níveis de pressão inseguros em um sistema.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A relief valve is a valve that is designed to automatically open at a predetermined pressure setpoint to relieve excess pressure and prevent unsafe pressure levels in a system.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (ReliefValve(x) ↔ (Valve(x) ∧ ∃f (PressureReliefFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every relief valve is a valve that bears a pressure relief function, which realizes a pressure relief process that automatically opens the valve when system pressure exceeds a predetermined setpoint.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">pressure relief valve</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b834">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000657"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000284">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A gas detector is a detector that has the designed function to sense the presence of a specified concentration of a gas.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(GasDetector(x) ↔ (Detector(x) ∧ ∃f(GasDetectionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1223"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A gas detector is a detector that has the designed function to sense the presence of a specified concentration of a gas.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um detector de gás é um detector que tem a função projetada de detectar a presença de uma concentração especificada de um gás.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gas detector</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">detector de gás</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every gas detector is a detector that bears a GasDetectionFunction and has a GasDetectingMeasuringElement as component part at all times.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000271">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A flame arrestor is a safety device that bears a flame arrest function to prevent flames from entering a system through an opening.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um arrestador de chama é um dispositivo de segurança que possui uma função de arrestar chama para prevenir que chamas entrem em um sistema através de uma abertura.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">arrestador de chama</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flame arrestor</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A flame arrestor is a safety device that bears a flame arrest function to prevent flames from entering a system through an opening.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(FlameArrestor(x) ↔ SafetyDevice(x) ∧ ∃f(FlameArrestFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1028"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every flame arrestor is a safety device that has the function of arresting flames and processes gaseous portions while preventing flame propagation.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1785">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000501">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2499"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b311"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b334"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2500"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1397"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1331"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1332"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b333"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b312"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b310"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b476"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1398"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b477"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a housing artifact creates and maintains a protective boundary around internal components, simultaneously providing structural support and environmental separation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a structural housing provides containment and protection for mechanical components, creating a defined boundary between internal mechanisms and the external environment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a housing or casing provides containment and protection for internal components, maintaining separation between the internal mechanism and external environment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a housing structure provides physical containment and environmental protection for internal components, shielding them from external conditions such as moisture, dust, mechanical impact, and temperature variations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a casing provides protective containment around internal components, maintaining their operational environment and structural integrity while allowing controlled access for maintenance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a casing provides protective containment around mechanical components while enabling controlled fluid passage through designed openings and maintaining pressure boundaries.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a body or housing artifact provides structural containment and protection for internal mechanical components or assemblies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a structural body provides containment and directional guidance for fluid flow while housing internal valve components that control the flow.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">enclosure process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de proteção e invólucro</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a structural body provides containment and directional guidance for fluid flow while housing internal valve components that control the flow.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a housing artifact creates and maintains a protective boundary around internal components, simultaneously providing structural support and environmental separation.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a structural housing provides containment and protection for mechanical components, creating a defined boundary between internal mechanisms and the external environment.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a housing or casing provides containment and protection for internal components, maintaining separation between the internal mechanism and external environment.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a housing structure provides physical containment and environmental protection for internal components, shielding them from external conditions such as moisture, dust, mechanical impact, and temperature variations.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a casing provides protective containment around internal components, maintaining their operational environment and structural integrity while allowing controlled access for maintenance.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a casing provides protective containment around mechanical components while enabling controlled fluid passage through designed openings and maintaining pressure boundaries.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a body or housing artifact provides structural containment and protection for internal mechanical components or assemblies.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000126">
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions because this is a constructive type defined by physical installation configuration. Under OWA, any filter with in-line connections and piping support could be classified as in-line filter, but specialized hybrid equipment or custom installations might have these features without belonging to the standard in-line filter maintenance category. Starting with necessary conditions protects against false positives.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (InLineFilter(x) → Filter(x) ∧ ∃m,e (InLineInstallation(m) ∧ ConnectedEquipment(e) ∧ hasInstallationMethod(x,m) ∧ supportedBy(x,e)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">filtro em linha</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">in line filter</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An in-line filter is a filter that is installed directly within a fluid line and supported by connected piping or equipment, designed to remove particles or contaminants from fluid streams during normal flow operations.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um filtro em linha é um filtro que é instalado diretamente dentro de uma linha de fluido e suportado por tubulações ou equipamentos conectados, projetado para remover partículas ou contaminantes de correntes de fluido durante operações normais de fluxo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An in-line filter is a filter that is installed directly within a fluid line and supported by connected piping or equipment, designed to remove particles or contaminants from fluid streams during normal flow operations.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000081"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1475"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every in-line filter is a filter that has an in-line installation method and is supported by connected equipment.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2192">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000627"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b749">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000179"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000304">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An injection pump is a pump that is specifically designed to inject fluid into reservoirs or production systems, typically at relatively high pressures.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1510"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(InjectionPump(x) ↔ Pump(x) ∧ ∃f(InjectionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An injection pump is a pump that is specifically designed to inject fluid into reservoirs or production systems, typically at relatively high pressures.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma bomba de injeção é uma bomba especificamente projetada para injetar fluido em reservatórios ou sistemas de produção, tipicamente em pressões relativamente altas.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">bomba de injeção</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">injection pump</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every injection pump is a pump that bears an injection function for delivering fluids to reservoirs or production systems.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b811">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b812"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000084"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2077">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000059"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000188">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2423"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2424"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the measurement and remote transmission of the temperature of a process stream or equipment surface.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de medição e transmissão de temperatura</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">temperature measurement and transmission function</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000551">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1441"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000616"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1442"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">hydraulic pumping process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de bombeamento hidráulico</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A pumping process in which mechanical energy is imparted to a hydraulic fluid to transmit power or actuate hydraulic equipment.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000191">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the movement of a gas stream from a region of lower pressure to a region of higher pressure.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b945"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b946"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de movimentação de gás</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gas movement function</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000168">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2175"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2176"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the release of excess pressure from a process system to a safe disposal location.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de ventilação de segurança</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">safety venting function</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000502">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b784"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b785"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the dispersion of thermal, acoustic, or kinetic energy over a larger volume or surface to reduce its local intensity.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de difusão de energia</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">energy diffusion function</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000118">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A flow transmitter is a transmitter that produces standardized output signals proportional to flow measurements from flow sensing elements.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1168"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um transmissor de fluxo é um transmissor que produz sinais de saída padronizados proporcionais às medições de fluxo provenientes de elementos sensores de fluxo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A flow transmitter is a transmitter that produces standardized output signals proportional to flow measurements from flow sensing elements.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1172"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flow transmitter</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">transmissor de fluxo</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1719">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000575"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b699">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000059"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1335">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000547"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000660">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b158"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which mechanical loads from attached components or piping are borne by a structural element to maintain their position and integrity.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de suporte</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supporting process</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000677">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tubing support function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de suporte de coluna de produção</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the mechanical suspension and support of downhole tubing strings within a wellbore.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2502"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2503"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000219">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b251"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Brake(x) ↔ (Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(BrakingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A brake is an assembly that bears a braking function to arrest or prevent the motion of an object, typically through friction or electromagnetic force application.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">freio</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">brake</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Brake</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">BRAKE</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um freio é um conjunto que possui uma função de frenagem para deter ou prevenir o movimento de um objeto, tipicamente através da aplicação de força de atrito ou eletromagnética.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A brake is an assembly that bears a braking function to arrest or prevent the motion of an object, typically through friction or electromagnetic force application.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every brake is an assembly that has the function of braking, and every assembly that has the function of braking is a brake.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1540">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000397"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000499">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b921"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b922"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which process flows or equipment are rapidly and automatically isolated in response to a detected hazardous condition.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de parada de emergência</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">emergency shut down process</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000521">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which the instantaneous flow rate of a process stream is measured and displayed locally or transmitted to a remote monitoring system.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1121"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1122"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de indicação de fluxo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flow indication process</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2140">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000066"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000670">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2455"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000195"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2454"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">three phase separation function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de separação trifásica</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A separation function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the separation of a gas–liquid hydrocarbon–produced water mixture into three distinct phases by gravity and residence time.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000281">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A furnace is a heater that bears the function to induce chemical reactions in process fluids through heating.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um forno é um aquecedor que possui a função de induzir reações químicas em fluidos de processo através do aquecimento.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">furnace</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">forno</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A furnace is a heater that bears the function to induce chemical reactions in process fluids through heating.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every furnace is a heater that has the function to induce reactions in process fluids by heating them.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Furnace(x) ↔ Heater(x) ∧ ∃f(ReactiveHeatingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1193"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1374">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b299">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasComponentPartAtAllTimes"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000444"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b395">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000694"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000639">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A material artifact that constitutes a lateral outlet port on a vessel or pipe fitting through which fluid is discharged from the side of the equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">saída lateral</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">side outlet</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2390">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2385"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2391"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1718">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000575"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000604">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transmitted from a driving component to a driven component through the rotation or linear motion of a shaft, enabling the transfer of torque and rotational speed.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transferred from a prime mover through a rotating shaft to one or more driven machines, typically involving the conversion of torque and rotational speed to match operational requirements.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transmitted through rotational motion from one component to another via a rotating shaft, enabling the transfer of torque and angular velocity to mounted components.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transmitted from an external energy source through a rotating shaft to downstream mechanical components, enabling power transfer within a mechanical system.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical rotational energy is transmitted from a prime mover through a shaft to driven components, resulting in the transfer of torque and rotational motion necessary for equipment operation.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical power is transferred from one rotating or reciprocating component to another through direct mechanical engagement, resulting in motion transmission and potentially torque or speed modification.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">power transmission process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de transmissão de potência</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transmitted from an external energy source through a rotating shaft to downstream mechanical components, enabling power transfer within a mechanical system.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical rotational energy is transmitted from a prime mover through a shaft to driven components, resulting in the transfer of torque and rotational motion necessary for equipment operation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical power is transferred from one rotating or reciprocating component to another through direct mechanical engagement, resulting in motion transmission and potentially torque or speed modification.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transmitted from a driving component to a driven component through the rotation or linear motion of a shaft, enabling the transfer of torque and rotational speed.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transferred from a prime mover through a rotating shaft to one or more driven machines, typically involving the conversion of torque and rotational speed to match operational requirements.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which mechanical energy is transmitted through rotational motion from one component to another via a rotating shaft, enabling the transfer of torque and angular velocity to mounted components.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b419">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000398"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000404">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de absorção</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">absorption process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b10"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b13"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b12"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b11"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which one or more gaseous components are transferred from a gas phase into a liquid absorbent phase through contact in petroleum production equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2115">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000525"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000266">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">cartucho de filtro</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">filter cartridge</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A filter cartridge is a filter that has a replaceable filter medium in a cartridge form factor designed for insertion into and removal from a filter housing.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b982"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000081"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um cartucho de filtro é um filtro que possui um meio filtrante substituível em formato de cartucho projetado para inserção e remoção de um alojamento de filtro.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A filter cartridge is a filter that has a replaceable filter medium in a cartridge form factor designed for insertion into and removal from a filter housing.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (FilterCartridge(x) → Filter(x) ∧ ∃m (ReplaceableFilterMedium(m) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,m)) ∧ ∃p (CartridgeGeometryProperty(p) ∧ bearerOf(x,p)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every filter cartridge is a filter that has a replaceable filter medium as component part and bears a cartridge geometry property.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type where the structural differentia (cartridge geometry and replaceability) is necessary but making it sufficient under OWA could lead to false positives - other equipment containing replaceable filter elements might be incorrectly classified as filter cartridges rather than their proper specialized categories.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000075">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">absorvedor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">absorber</rdfs:label>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b14"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every absorber is a pressure vessel that has a gas-absorption function whose realization absorbs specific components from a fluid mixture through mass transfer to an absorbent phase</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An absorber is a pressure vessel that realizes an absorption function for selective mass transfer of components from a fluid mixture into an absorbent phase.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um absorvedor é um vaso de pressão que realiza uma função de absorção para transferência seletiva de massa de componentes de uma mistura fluida para uma fase absorvente.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An absorber is a pressure vessel that realizes an absorption function for selective mass transfer of components from a fluid mixture into an absorbent phase.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Absorber(x) ↔ (PressureVessel(x) ∧ ∃f(GasAbsorptionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000598">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">pig de pipeline</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pipeline pig</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A material artifact that constitutes a device inserted into and propelled through a pipeline to perform internal inspection, cleaning, or gauging operations.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000199">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in an ElectricalPowerTransformationProcess and that consists in converting electrical energy from one voltage level to another through electromagnetic induction, enabling power distribution and utilization at appropriate voltage levels.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in an ElectricalPowerTransformationProcess and that consists in changing the voltage and current levels of electrical power through electromagnetic induction while maintaining power transfer efficiency.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de transformação de energia elétrica</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">electrical power transformation function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1978"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2476"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1974"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1979"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2475"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1983"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1982"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1975"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in an ElectricalPowerTransformationProcess and that consists in converting electrical energy from one voltage level to another through electromagnetic induction, enabling power distribution and utilization at appropriate voltage levels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in an ElectricalPowerTransformationProcess and that consists in changing the voltage and current levels of electrical power through electromagnetic induction while maintaining power transfer efficiency.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000371">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">valve seat</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">assento de válvula</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Valve seat is a constructive type defined by its structural configuration and interface role. Under the Open World Assumption, making this an equivalence class could lead to false positives where any artifact that is part of a valve and adjacent to a closure member gets classified as a valve seat, even if it serves a different structural role (such as guides, stops, or supports).</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2605"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2606"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A MaterialArtifact that is part of a valve and that provides the seating surface against which the closure member bears to achieve shut-off and control of process fluid flow.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um MaterialArtifact que é parte de uma válvula e que fornece a superfície de assentamento contra a qual o membro de fechamento se apoia para alcançar o fechamento e controle do fluxo de fluido de processo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A MaterialArtifact that is part of a valve and that provides the seating surface against which the closure member bears to achieve shut-off and control of process fluid flow.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000512">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000548"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1015"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1017"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1018"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1016"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1019"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A heating process in which thermal energy is generated by the combustion of fuel and transferred to a process stream or vessel through a fired heater.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">fired heating process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de aquecimento a combustão</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000574">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1230"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b928"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b927"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1719"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1718"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1229"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1432"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b734"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1431"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b733"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">mechanical energy generation function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de geração de energia mecânica</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the conversion of thermal, chemical, or electrical energy into mechanical energy in the form of rotational or linear motion.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1576">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000564"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000323">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A pipe elbow is a pipe that has curved geometry enabling directional changes in pipe runs between 0 and 135 degrees.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um cotovelo de tubulação é uma tubulação que possui geometria curva permitindo mudanças direcionais em trechos de tubulação entre 0 e 135 graus.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every pipe elbow is a pipe that has curved geometry and enables directional change capacity between 0 and 135 degrees.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A pipe elbow is a pipe that has curved geometry enabling directional changes in pipe runs between 0 and 135 degrees.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions for this constructive type protects against false positives under OWA. Any curved piping component would be forcibly classified as a pipe elbow under equivalent axioms, including specialized equipment like coiled tubing, serpentine heat exchanger tubes, or custom manifold sections that contain curved passages but should not be asserted into the standard pipe elbow maintenance category.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000321"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1853"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">cotovelo de tubulação</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pipe elbow</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (PipeElbow(x) → (Pipe(x) ∧ ∃g(CurvedGeometry(g) ∧ hasGeometricProperty(x,g)) ∧ ∃p(DirectionalChangeCapacity(p) ∧ hasProperty(x,p))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2402">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000047"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000602">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A measurement process in which the position of a mechanical component is measured and the corresponding signal transmitted to a remote control or monitoring system.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000572"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1950"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1951"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de medição e transmissão de posição</rdfs:label>
