  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000320">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A pig trap is an assembly that bears the function of launching and receiving pipe pigs for pipeline maintenance and has both launcher and receiver components.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma armadilha de pig é um conjunto que possui a função de lançar e receber pigs de tubulação para manutenção de dutos e possui componentes de lançador e receptor.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A pig trap is an assembly that bears the function of launching and receiving pipe pigs for pipeline maintenance and has both launcher and receiver components.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">armadilha de pig</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pig trap</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every pig trap is an assembly that bears a pig launching and receiving function and has component parts that are a pig launcher and a pig receiver.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1813"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(PigTrap(x) ↔ Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(PigLaunchingAndReceivingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃l(PigLauncher(l) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,l)) ∧ ∃r(PigReceiver(r) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,r)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000377">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um cabeçal de poço é um conjunto que porta uma função de controle superficial do poço e fornece a interface estrutural e de controle entre um poço e os equipamentos de superfície.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A wellhead is an assembly that bears a well surface control function and provides the structural and control interface between a wellbore and surface equipment.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A wellhead is an assembly that bears a well surface control function and provides the structural and control interface between a wellbore and surface equipment.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2680"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Wellhead(x) ↔ Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(WellSurfaceControlFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃h(CasingHanger(h) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,h)) ∧ ∃w(Wellbore(w) ∧ hasConnectionTo(x,w)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">wellhead</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">cabeçal de poço</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every wellhead is an assembly that bears a well surface control function and has component parts including casing hangers and connection to wellbore</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b560">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000442"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b474">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000501"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b942">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000668"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000513">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1025"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1024"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de contenção de chama</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flame arrest function</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the prevention of flame propagation through a flammable gas mixture by quenching the flame front in narrow passages.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1894">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000161"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000342">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">rotor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">rotor</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An Assembly that participates in rotational motion and has a rotor shaft as an essential component, designed to transfer mechanical energy through rotational motion within a machine assembly.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um Assembly que participa em movimento rotacional e tem um eixo do rotor como componente essencial, projetado para transferir energia mecânica através de movimento rotacional dentro de um conjunto de máquina.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An Assembly that participates in rotational motion and has a rotor shaft as an essential component, designed to transfer mechanical energy through rotational motion within a machine assembly.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2149"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2148"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">As a constructive type defined by physical configuration (rotating portion with shaft), providing sufficient conditions under OWA could lead to overclassification. Complex assemblies containing rotating elements might be incorrectly classified as rotors rather than their proper categories (motors, compressors, etc.).</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b402">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasComponentPartAtAllTimes"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/WingValve"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b891">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b892"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/GasDetectingMeasuringElement">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gas detecting measuring element</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">elemento de medição de detecção de gás</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A material artifact that constitutes a sensing element within petroleum production gas detection equipment that responds to the presence and concentration of a target gas.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000573"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000248">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">atuador de diafragma</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">diaphragm actuator</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000207"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b698"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b699"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Classification basis is constructive - identity given by diaphragm mechanism. Under OWA, sufficient conditions would force any equipment with a diaphragm component to be classified as a diaphragm actuator, potentially including complex hybrid systems or custom equipment where the diaphragm serves auxiliary functions. Starting with necessary conditions protects against such false positives.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um atuador de diafragma é um atuador que utiliza um diafragma como componente essencial para converter sinais de controle em movimento mecânico ou força para operar outros equipamentos.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A diaphragm actuator is an actuator that uses a diaphragm as an essential component for converting control signals into mechanical motion or force to operate other equipment.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A diaphragm actuator is an actuator that uses a diaphragm as an essential component for converting control signals into mechanical motion or force to operate other equipment.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b53">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b50"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b54"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000068">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2266"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b58"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1899"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1353"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1365"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1004"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1005"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b59"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1898"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1354"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2265"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1364"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heat transfer function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de transferência de calor</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in a HeatTransferProcess and that consists in facilitating the transfer of thermal energy between two or more fluid media while maintaining their physical separation.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in a HeatTransferProcess and that consists in facilitating the transfer of thermal energy between two or more fluid media while maintaining their physical separation.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2303">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2305"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1689">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000569"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b240">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000568"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000346">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An Assembly that bears a PowerTransmissionFunction and that has component parts including shaft keys for torque transmission and shaft seals for leakage prevention, serving as the core rotating element in rotating machinery.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um Assembly que porta uma PowerTransmissionFunction e que possui partes componentes incluindo chavetas de eixo para transmissão de torque e vedações de eixo para prevenção de vazamento, servindo como o elemento rotativo central em máquinas rotativas.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2238"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2239"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An Assembly that bears a PowerTransmissionFunction and that has component parts including shaft keys for torque transmission and shaft seals for leakage prevention, serving as the core rotating element in rotating machinery.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">eixo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">shaft</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification based on physical structure. Under OWA, sufficient conditions for shaft identity could lead to false positives - any assembly with a shaft key and rotational motion might be classified as a shaft rather than a more specific equipment type that contains a shaft. The structural differentia provides necessary conditions while allowing domain experts to validate sufficiency.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2245">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000636"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1609">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b559">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000174"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1314">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000027"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2455">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000671"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000372">
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type defined by physical structure (rod/shaft mechanism). Under Open World Assumption, sufficient conditions would force any assembly with a valve stem seal and force transmission function to be classified as a valve stem, which could include complex multi-component assemblies, manifolds, or specialized valve mechanisms that contain these elements but should not be asserted into the standard valve stem maintenance category.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An Assembly that bears a ForceTransmissionFunction and that has a valve stem seal as a component part, specifically designed to transmit motion from a valve operator to the valve closure member.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um Assembly que porta uma ForceTransmissionFunction e que tem um selo de haste de válvula como parte componente, especificamente projetado para transmitir movimento de um operador de válvula para o membro de fechamento da válvula.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An Assembly that bears a ForceTransmissionFunction and that has a valve stem seal as a component part, specifically designed to transmit motion from a valve operator to the valve closure member.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2609"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2610"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">haste de válvula</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">valve stem</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000247">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A dew point analyser is an instrument that bears a dew point measurement function.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">analisador de ponto de orvalho</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">dew point analyser</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um analisador de ponto de orvalho é um instrumento que possui uma função de medição de ponto de orvalho.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A dew point analyser is an instrument that bears a dew point measurement function.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b682"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every dew point analyser is an instrument that has the function to determine the dew point of a substance</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(DewPointAnalyser(x) ↔ Instrument(x) ∧ ∃f(DewPointMeasurementFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1296">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000604"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1721">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000574"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000280">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A flowline is a pipeline that transports oil, gas, or water directly from a wellhead to a manifold or production facility.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma linha de fluxo é um duto que transporta óleo, gás ou água diretamente de uma cabeça de poço para um manifold ou instalação de produção.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A flowline is a pipeline that transports oil, gas, or water directly from a wellhead to a manifold or production facility.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every flowline is a pipeline that bears a fluid transport function, has a wellhead connection, has a manifold or production facility connection, and transports hydrocarbon fluids.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flowline</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">linha de fluxo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1186"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000326"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Flowline(x) ↔ Pipeline(x) ∧ ∃f(FluidTransportFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃w(Wellhead(w) ∧ connectsDirectly(x,w)) ∧ ∃m((Manifold(m) ∨ ProductionFacility(m)) ∧ connectsDirectly(x,m)) ∧ ∃h(HydrocarbonFluid(h) ∧ hasInput(x,h)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2531">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000355">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um MaterialArtifact que possui uma StationaryMachineComponentFunction e que é o componente estrutural estacionário dentro de máquinas rotativas, fornecendo alojamento e estabilidade posicional para elementos ativos como bobinas, palhetas ou vedações.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A MaterialArtifact that bears a StationaryMachineComponentFunction and that is the stationary structural component within rotating machinery, providing housing and positional stability for active elements such as windings, vanes, or seals.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">stator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">MaterialArtifact que possui uma StationaryMachineComponentFunction e</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Stator(x) → MaterialArtifact(x) ∧ ∃f(StationaryMachineComponentFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃m(RotatingMachine(m) ∧ partOf(x,m)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification based on structural positioning within rotating machinery. Under OWA, any artifact described as stationary within a rotating machine context could be classified as a stator, but this may include specialized hybrid components, mounting structures, or custom configurations that should not be automatically asserted into the standard stator maintenance category. The structural differentia (stationary positioning) is necessary but making it sufficient requires domain expert validation.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2345"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2344"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A MaterialArtifact that bears a StationaryMachineComponentFunction and that is the stationary structural component within rotating machinery, providing housing and positional stability for active elements such as windings, vanes, or seals.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every Stator is a MaterialArtifact that bears a StationaryMachineComponentFunction and is part of some RotatingMachine</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b10">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000044"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b483">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000038"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1029">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000513"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000315">
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every motor is an assembly that has the function of generating mechanical energy and has as output rotational kinetic energy.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A motor is an assembly that bears a mechanical energy generation function to convert electrical, chemical, pneumatic, or hydraulic energy into rotational mechanical energy.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Motor(x) ↔ Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(MechanicalEnergyGenerationFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃e(RotationalKineticEnergy(e) ∧ hasOutput(x,e)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">motor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">motor</rdfs:label>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1720"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A motor is an assembly that bears a mechanical energy generation function to convert electrical, chemical, pneumatic, or hydraulic energy into rotational mechanical energy.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um motor é um conjunto que possui uma função de geração de energia mecânica para converter energia elétrica, química, pneumática ou hidráulica em energia mecânica rotacional.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b879">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000407"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2421">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2422"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000636">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de agitação mecânica</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">shaking function</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the application of oscillating mechanical motion to a screen or separator to promote separation of solids from a fluid.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2240"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2241"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000593">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de lançamento de pig</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pig launching process</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1784"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1785"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1787"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1786"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which a pipeline pig is introduced into a pipeline under operating pressure to perform internal cleaning, inspection, or product separation.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2004">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000633">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">elemento de sensoriamento</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sensing element</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A material artifact that constitutes a primary element that directly responds to a physical or chemical variable to generate a measurement signal in petroleum production instrumentation.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000123">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula globo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">globe valve</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions for this constructive type. Under OWA, making the structural differentia sufficient could force classification of specialized equipment containing linear motion closures (like complex multi-way valves or custom manifolds) as standard globe valves when they may warrant distinct maintenance categories.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A globe valve is a valve characterized by a closure member (disc or plug) that operates with linear motion perpendicular to a seat that is oriented normal to the fluid flow path.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula globo é uma válvula caracterizada por um elemento de fechamento (disco ou tampão) que opera com movimento linear perpendicular a uma sede orientada normal ao caminho do fluxo do fluido.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000077"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1328"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A globe valve is a valve characterized by a closure member (disc or plug) that operates with linear motion perpendicular to a seat that is oriented normal to the fluid flow path.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every globe valve is a valve that has as component part at all times a linear motion closure and a normal seat.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(GlobeValve(x) → Valve(x) ∧ ∃y,z(hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,y) ∧ LinearMotionClosure(y) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,z) ∧ NormalSeat(z)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000495">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which two or more electrical conductor parts are held in intimate contact by an electrical connector, resulting in a conductive path that enables electrical current flow through the connection.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de conexão elétrica</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">electrical connection process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which two or more electrical conductor parts are held in intimate contact by an electrical connector, resulting in a conductive path that enables electrical current flow through the connection.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000360">
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2453"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">thin plate</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">Placa que possui geometria de espessura fina e</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(ThinPlate(x) → Plate(x) ∧ ∃q1(ThinThickness(q1) ∧ hasQuality(x,q1)) ∧ ∃q2(ColdFormedManufacturing(q2) ∧ hasQuality(x,q2)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A Plate that has thin thickness geometry and is manufactured through cold forming processes, typically used for structural support applications requiring reduced weight or specific geometric constraints.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A Plate that has thin thickness geometry and is manufactured through cold forming processes, typically used for structural support applications requiring reduced weight or specific geometric constraints.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma Placa que possui geometria de espessura fina e é fabricada através de processos de conformação a frio, tipicamente usada para aplicações de suporte estrutural que requerem peso reduzido ou restrições geométricas específicas.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type defined by physical geometry (thinness) and manufacturing method (cold forming). Under OWA, sufficient conditions for thin plates are difficult to specify without risking false positives from specialized hybrid structures that contain thin cold-formed elements but should not be classified as standard thin plates.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">ThinPlate ⊑ Plate ⊓ ∃hasQuality.ThinThickness ⊓ ∃hasQuality.ColdFormedManufacturing</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000446">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">indicador de controle</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">control indicator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A material artifact that constitutes a component that displays and enables adjustment of a set point or control parameter in petroleum production equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000136">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma placa de orifício é um elemento de medição de fluxo que consiste de uma placa fina com um orifício especificado através do qual o fluido flui para criar pressão diferencial para medição da taxa de fluxo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An orifice plate is a flow element that consists of a thin plate with a specified hole through which fluid flows to create differential pressure for flow rate measurement.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000116"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1757"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1756"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every orifice plate is a flow element that has a thin plate component and has a specified hole component and bears a flow measurement function.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An orifice plate is a flow element that consists of a thin plate with a specified hole through which fluid flows to create differential pressure for flow rate measurement.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">placa de orifício</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">orifice plate</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification based on physical structure. Under OWA, any plate with a hole could potentially be classified as an orifice plate, but many perforated plates serve different purposes (structural, filtering, etc.). The structural differentia alone is not sufficient without industrial context validation.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(OrificePlate(x) → FlowMeasuringElement(x) ∧ ∃p,h(ThinPlate(p) ∧ SpecifiedHole(h) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,p) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,h)) ∧ ∃f(FlowMeasurementFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1191">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2658">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000656"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000364">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tubing hanger</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">suporte de coluna de produção</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A tubing hanger is an assembly that supports tubing strings in wellheads with integrated sealing to isolate tubing conduit from annulus.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2506"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every tubing hanger is an assembly that bears a tubing support function and has component parts including a sealing system, support mechanism, and tubing connection.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(TubingHanger(x) ↔ (Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(TubingSupportFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃s(SealingSystem(s) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,s)) ∧ ∃m(SupportMechanism(m) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,m)) ∧ ∃c(TubingConnection(c) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,c))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um suporte de coluna de produção é um conjunto que suporta colunas de produção em cabeças de poço com vedação integrada para isolar o conduto da coluna do anular.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A tubing hanger is an assembly that supports tubing strings in wellheads with integrated sealing to isolate tubing conduit from annulus.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2405">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2406"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000091"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b2059">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ne8179f87f39249a5b317c58c25587df2b1137">
